'''''Marvel's Guardians of the Galaxy''''', known as '''''Marvel's Guardians of the Galaxy: Mission Breakout''''' for the final season, is an American [[animated television series]] based on the [[Marvel Comics]] superhero team [[Guardians of the Galaxy (2008 team)|of the same name]]. It is produced by [[Marvel Animation]]. The series premiered on September 5, 2015, on [[Disney XD]].

''Marvel's Guardians of the Galaxy'' features the same main characters as the [[Guardians of the Galaxy (film)|film of the same name]], although it is not a part of the [[Marvel Cinematic Universe]].<ref name="slf" /> [[Seth Green]] was the only actor from the film to return, reprising his voice role as [[Howard the Duck]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Prom |first=Bradley |date=August 19, 2022 |title=Marvel: 10 Best Animated TV Series, Ranked According To IMDb |url=https://screenrant.com/marvel-best-animated-tv-shows-imdb/ |access-date=2023-08-26 |website=[[Screen Rant]] |language=en}}</ref>

The third and final season premiered in March 2018,<ref name="D23 Expo">{{cite web|last=Pedersen|first=Erik|title='Marvel's Spider-Man': Premiere Date & Voice Cast Set For Disney XD Toon Series|url=https://deadline.com/2017/07/marvels-spider-man-premiere-date-voice-cast-disney-xd-d23-1202129382/|work=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|access-date=February 24, 2020|date=July 15, 2017}}</ref> and ended on June 9, 2019.<ref>{{cite web|title=MARVEL'S GUARDIANS OF THE GALAXY (DISNEY XD)|url=http://www.thefutoncritic.com/showatch/marvels-guardians-of-the-galaxy/listings/|work=[[The Futon Critic]]|access-date=February 24, 2020}}</ref>

==Plot==
===Season 1===
The [[Guardians of the Galaxy (2008 team)|Guardians of the Galaxy]] team consists of [[Star-Lord]], [[Gamora]], [[Drax the Destroyer]], [[Rocket Raccoon]], and [[Groot]]. During season one, the Guardians obtain an artifact called the Spartaxian CryptoCube that is tied to the Spartax species. The Cube contains a map leading to the Cosmic Seed, a powerful weapon capable of creating a new universe. The Guardians must find and destroy the Cosmic Seed before it can be weaponized for evil.

===Season 2===
Season two starts with the Guardians teaming up with the [[Avengers (comics)|Avengers]] to fight the [[High Evolutionary]].<ref>{{cite tweet|user=Marvel|number=835942517120061443|title=ICYMI: The Guardians and Avengers team up for the Season 2 premiere of "Marvel's Guardians of the Galaxy"! Details: https://t.co/4NjitgpY6a https://t.co/sD3z0cIkqb|date=February 27, 2017|author=Marvel Entertainment|access-date=February 24, 2020}}</ref>

Following [[Thanos]]'s defeat, the Guardians get their hands on a sarcophagus that was found on Thanos's asteroid base and stolen by [[Yondu]]. This sarcophagus later hatches into [[Adam Warlock]], who the Guardians convince to follow his own destiny.

Star-Lord's father [[J'son (character)|J'son]], the king of the Spartax and the leader of the [[Universal Church of Truth|Universal Believers]], escapes prison and uses [[Nova Corps]] helmets to control Adam and transform him into the [[Adam Warlock#The Magus|Magus]]. The Guardians break J'son out of Magus, restoring him to normal.

===Season 3: Mission Breakout===
In the third season, the Guardians go on the run after being framed by the [[Collector (character)|Collector]]. [[Phyla-Vell]] works with the Guardians to save the [[Kree]] homeworld of Hala and defeat the Collector, who escapes after setting his ship to self-destruct.<ref name="D23 Expo"/>

After traversing through the [[Black Vortex]], the Guardians discover that the Asgardians' old enemies the [[Darkhawk]]s have been replacing [[Irani Rael|Nova Prime]] and members of the Galactic Council. The Darkhawks are made by [[Serpent (character)|Serpent]], who plans to reclaim [[Asgard (comics)|Asgard]]. Using the [[Dragonfang]] sword, the Guardians defeat Serpent and save the galaxy.

Season three included Marvel characters [[Spider-Man]], [[Max Modell]], [[Venom (character)|Venom]], and [[Carnage (character)|Carnage]] in a crossover with the television series ''[[Spider-Man (2017 TV series)|Spider-Man]]'', and had [[Stan Lee]] in a guest role.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Johnston |first=Rich |author-link=Rich Johnston |date=October 8, 2017 |title=Stan Lee to Play a Character in Guardians of the Galaxy/Ultimate Spider-Man Cartoon Crossover |url=https://www.bleedingcool.com/2017/10/08/stan-lee-character-guardians-galaxy-ultimate-spider-man-cartoon-crossover/ |website=[[Bleeding Cool]]}}</ref>

