==Production==
Marvel was rumored to be considering a new animated series with another ''Spider-Man'' show or a ''Guardians of the Galaxy'' show. The appearances of the ''Guardians of the Galaxy'' in ''[[Avengers Assemble (TV series)|Avengers Assemble]]'' and ''[[Ultimate Spider-Man (TV series)|Ultimate Spider-Man]]'' were supposed to be test runs for their own show. Screen Rant indicated in January 2014 that the ''Guardians of the Galaxy'' series was selected for development.<ref>{{cite news|last1=Shaw-Williams|first1=H.|title=Rumor Patrol: 'Guardians of the Galaxy' Animated Series in Development at Marvel|url=https://screenrant.com/guardians-of-the-galaxy-cartoon-animated-series-marvel/|access-date=June 2, 2015|work=ScreenRant|date=January 3, 2014}}</ref>

On July 26, 2014, at [[San Diego Comic-Con]], a week before the release of the ''[[Guardians of the Galaxy (film)|Guardians of the Galaxy]]'' film, Marvel Animation announced the Guardians of the Galaxy animated TV series with a trailer featuring Rocket Raccoon and Star-Lord.<ref name="ComicCon" /> With the success of the live-action film, Marvel and Disney XD announced that they were moving forward with the animated series at [[New York Comic Con]]. They showed some test footage to the audience.<ref name=vty/> The series was announced to air in 2015 as a part of the Marvel Universe on [[Disney XD]].<ref name="RevealTHR" />

Advanced previews of the show started airing on Disney XD on August 1, 2015. A full preview of the series aired on Disney XD on September 5, 2015. The official one-hour premiere aired on September 26, 2015.<ref name=cartoon>{{cite news|url=https://www.bcdb.com/blog/guardians-of-the-galaxy-release-imminent|title=Guardians of the Galaxy Release Imminent|first=Dave|last=Koch|publisher=Big Cartoon News|date=August 2, 2015|access-date=August 2, 2015}}</ref>

Each episode is named after or a reference to a popular song from the 1960s, 1970s, or 1980s.

At New York Comic Con 2015, it was announced the series had been renewed for a second season, which premiered on Disney XD on March 11, 2017.<ref>{{Cite web|title=NYCC 2015: Disney XD Renews Marvel's 'Guardians of the Galaxy'|url=http://marvel.com/news/tv/25259/nycc_2015_disney_xd_renews_marvels_guardians_of_the_galaxy|date=October 9, 2015|website=Marvel|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20151012222854/http://marvel.com/news/tv/25259/nycc_2015_disney_xd_renews_marvels_guardians_of_the_galaxy|archive-date=October 12, 2015}}</ref>

==Music==
In late August, it was revealed that licensed songs from the 1970s would be used to augment the tone and soundtrack of the series.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Johnston |first=Rich |author-link=Rich Johnston |date=2015-08-25 |title=Guardians Of The Galaxy Cartoon Licenses Real 70s Hits, Like The Movie (UPDATE) |url=https://bleedingcool.com/movies/guardians-of-the-galaxy-cartoon-licenses-real-70s-hits-like-the-movie/ |access-date=2023-01-06 |website=[[Bleeding Cool]] |language=en}}</ref>

In September, ''Marvel's Guardians of the Galaxy: Cosmic Mix Vol. 1 (Music from the Animated Television Series)'' was announced. It is a collection of 12 songs featured in the show's first season.<ref>{{Cite web |date=September 14, 2015 |title=Marvel Music Presents 'Cosmic Mix Vol. 1,' Out on October 16 |url=https://marvel.com/news/tv/25080/marvel_music_presents_cosmic_mix_vol_1_out_on_october_16 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150918020046/https://marvel.com/news/tv/25080/marvel_music_presents_cosmic_mix_vol_1_out_on_october_16 |archive-date=September 18, 2015 |website=[[Marvel.com]]}}</ref>

