==Broadcast==
''Guardians of the Galaxy'' aired as a preview on Disney XD in the United States and [[Disney Channel (Canada)|Disney Channel]] in Canada on September 5, 2015. It officially debuted on September 26, 2015.<ref name="DisneyCanadaStart" /> The series premiered on [[Disney XD (UK & Ireland)|Disney XD]] in the United Kingdom and Ireland on November 7, 2015. It also premiered on [[Disney XD (Australia and New Zealand)|Disney XD]] in Australia and New Zealand on November 8, 2015.<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.entertainment-focus.com/tv-section/tv-news/marvels-guardians-of-the-galaxy-coming-to-disney-xd/|title=Marvel's Guardians of the Galaxy coming to Disney XD|last=Ellwood|first=Greg|date=15 October 2015|work=Entertainment Focus|access-date=18 October 2015}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |author=DisneyXDAU |date=October 9, 2015 |title=#GuardiansoftheGalaxy will premiere 8 Nov in AUNZ on @Foxtel |url=https://twitter.com/DisneyXD_AU/status/652713254628683776 |access-date=October 18, 2015 |work=[[Twitter]]}}</ref> In India, from March 8, 2019, it is being aired on [[Marvel HQ]], an Indian version of [[Disney XD (Indian TV channel)|Disney XD]].

==Reception==

===Critical response===
The [[review aggregator]] website [[Rotten Tomatoes]] reports an 86% approval rating with an average rating of 7.00/10, based on 7 reviews for the first season.<ref>{{cite web |title=Marvel's Guardians of the Galaxy: Season 1 |url=https://www.rottentomatoes.com/tv/marvel_s_guardians_of_the_galaxy/s01 |access-date=2020-10-01 |website=[[Rotten Tomatoes]]}}</ref>

Blair Marnell of ''[[Nerdist]]'' called "Road to Knowhere" a "pretty solid introduction to the ''Guardians of the Galaxy'' animated series," saying, "Of course, there's always room for improvement. If ''Guardians of the Galaxy'' is really going to be a standalone franchise, then it needs this animated series to keep going all the way up to the next movie in 2017. This show might be good enough to do that."<ref name="Nerdist">{{cite web |last=Marnell |first=Blair |date=September 6, 2015 |title=Guardians of the Galaxy Animated Series Review: "Road to Knowhere" |url=https://archive.nerdist.com/guardians-of-the-galaxy-animated-series-review-road-to-knowhere/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20151121075241/http://nerdist.com/guardians-of-the-galaxy-animated-series-review-road-to-knowhere/ |archive-date=November 21, 2015 |access-date=November 21, 2015 |website=[[Nerdist]]}}</ref> David Griffin of ''[[Screen Rant]]'' stated that the premiere of the show delivers an "exhilarating action-packed adventure," asserting, "Now we just have to see if the exciting action and engaging storylines can stay strong throughout the entire season."<ref>{{Cite web |last=Griffin |first=David |date=September 27, 2015 |title=Guardians of the Galaxy Series Premiere Review: Hooked on a Feeling |url=https://screenrant.com/guardians-of-the-galaxy-disney-xd-premiere-review/ |access-date=2023-08-26 |website=[[Screen Rant]] |language=en}}</ref> Kevin Johnson of ''[[The A.V. Club]]'' gave "Knowhere to Run" a B+ ranking and "Road to Knowhere" a B− ranking, writing, "Disney XD has a very specific demographic they're aiming for, which leaves "Road to Knowhere/Knowhere to Run" somewhat clunky and awkward, but brimming with potential and leaves you eager for more. The two-part pilot is simultaneously complicated and simplistic, struggling to give the story and its characters due weight while forcing some unnecessary exposition and comic beats that even the show feels embarrassed by. But when it works, it works (particularly in the second half), and those small moments make the show worthwhile."<ref>{{Cite web |date=2015-09-27 |title=Guardians Of The Galaxy: "Road To Knowhere/Knowhere To Run" |url=https://www.avclub.com/guardians-of-the-galaxy-road-to-knowhere-knowhere-to-1798184986 |access-date=2023-08-26 |website=The A.V. Club |language=en}}</ref>

Jesse Schedeen of ''[[IGN]]'' gave the series a grade of seven out of ten, stating, "The good news is that the second episode of Guardians of the Galaxy improved a bit on the first. More screen time for Cosmo certainly didn't hurt, but it was also a matter of the show tapping into the group dynamic and their dysfunctional but close bond a little more. The show continues to frustrate in just how aggressively similar it is to the movie, but with the groundwork now laid and the promise of Star-Lord's heritage being a major focus going forward, hopefully the show can begin to define itself on its own merits."<ref>{{Cite web |last=Schedeen |first=Jesse |date=September 27, 2015 |title=Marvel's Guardians of the Galaxy: "Knowhere to Run" Review |url=https://www.ign.com/articles/2015/09/27/marvels-guardians-of-the-galaxy-knowhere-to-run-review |access-date=2023-08-26 |website=[[IGN]] |language=en}}</ref> James Whitbrook of ''[[Gizmodo]]'' said that ''Guardians of the Galaxy'' has "gone from disappointing to delightful."<ref>{{Cite web |last=Whitbrook |first=James |date=October 27, 2015 |title=The Guardians of the Galaxy TV Show Finally Got Good |url=https://gizmodo.com/the-guardians-of-the-galaxy-tv-show-finally-got-good-1739020620 |access-date=2023-08-26 |website=[[Gizmodo]] |language=en}}</ref> Emily Ashby of ''[[Common Sense Media]]'' gave ''Marvel's Guardians of the Galaxy'' a grade of four out of five stars, noted the depiction of positive messages and role models across the characters, citing teamwork and altruism, and asserted, "Ragtag hero bunch's continuing story is violent but fun."<ref>{{Cite web |last=Ashby |first=Emily |title=Marvel's Guardians of the Galaxy TV Review {{!}} Common Sense Media |url=https://www.commonsensemedia.org/tv-reviews/marvels-guardians-of-the-galaxy |access-date=2023-08-26 |website=[[Common Sense Media]] |language=en}}</ref>

Joseph Ocasio of ''[[Comic Book Resources]]'' ranked ''Guardians of the Galaxy'' 8th in their "Best Marvel Animated Series" list, writing, "While the cartoon Guardians were not as fleshed out as their big-screen counterparts, the show captured most of what made the Guardians such wonderful characters. Star-Lord was still the lovable numbskull with a heart of gold, and Rocket was still the short-tempered rodent."<ref>{{Cite web |last=Ocasio |first=Joseph |date=June 27, 2023 |title=The Best Marvel Animated Series |url=https://www.cbr.com/top-best-marvel-animated-tv-series/ |access-date=2023-08-26 |website=[[Comic Book Resources]] |language=en}}</ref> Judy Black of ''[[Collider (website)|Collider]]'' ranked ''Marvel's Guardians of the Galaxy'' 9th in their "12 Best Marvel Animated Series Not in the MCU" list, saying, "As people often point out, there are many fantastic aspects of animation that live-action adaptations simply cannot replicate. The quick and fluid movements, for instance, lead to some impressive gags that capture the personalities of the more eccentric characters, like Quill/Star-Lord. Additionally, Will Friedle does a fantastic job voicing Star-Lord, perhaps portraying him as a little less serious than his live-action counterpart. This cartoon was intended for kids, and oftentimes, it shows, particularly with its sometimes-predictable humor. Still, it offers many good laughs for the whole family."<ref>{{Cite web |last=Black |first=Judy |date=August 27, 2022 |title=The 12 Best Marvel Animated Series Not in the MCU, Ranked |url=https://collider.com/best-marvel-animated-series-ranked/ |access-date=2023-08-26 |website=[[Collider (website)|Collider]] |language=en}}</ref>

