== In other media ==
In 2015, ''Marvel's Guardians of the Galaxy'' was adapted into a comic book series known as ''Marvel Universe: Guardians of the Galaxy''.<ref>{{Cite web |last=McMillan |first=Graeme |date=November 13, 2014 |title=Kid-Friendly 'Marvel Universe: Guardians of the Galaxy' Comic Launching in 2015 |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/news/general-news/kid-friendly-marvel-universe-guardians-748808/ |access-date=2023-08-26 |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]] |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Burlingame |first=Russ |date=November 13, 2014 |title=Guardians Of The Galaxy All Ages Title Announced By Marvel |url=https://comicbook.com/marvel/news/guardians-of-the-galaxy-all-ages-title-announced-by-marvel/ |access-date=2023-08-26 |website=[[ComicBook.com]] |language=en}}</ref> It uses the episode's art work with writing and lettering by Joe Caramagna.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Schedeen |first=Jesse |date=November 13, 2014 |title=Marvel Announces New Guardians of the Galaxy Comic |url=https://www.ign.com/articles/2014/11/13/marvel-announces-new-guardians-of-the-galaxy-comic |access-date=2023-08-26 |website=[[IGN]] |language=en}}</ref> The first issue was released in February 2015.<ref>{{Cite web |last=MacDonald |first=Heidi |date=November 18, 2014 |title=Marvel's February 2015 Solicitations: Star Wars is coming |url=https://www.comicsbeat.com/marvels-february-2015-solicitations-star-wars-is-coming/ |access-date=2023-08-26 |website=[[ComicsBeat]] |language=en-US}}</ref>

